"description":"You are never too old to learn something new.\n\nOld Dog helps adults build useful understanding through focused lessons, practice and proof of learning. Explore a subject, find a starting point and return to your saved place whenever you have a few minutes.\n\nTEN COURSES TO EXPLORE\nStart with personal finance, credit and debt, economics, artificial intelligence, computer literacy, cybersecurity, professional communication, cooking, home maintenance or critical thinking. Each course has a clear purpose, two units and four learning objectives. For new users, the first course in each of Money, Technology, Career, Life Skills and Humanities is free. People who used Old Dog before 1.2 keep all ten current courses. A one-time unlock opens all courses, including subjects added later.\n\nLEARN, PRACTISE, DEMONSTRATE\nRead a concise lesson and a worked example. Practise with feedback that explains the reasoning. Then apply the idea in two new situations. Correct practice and both correct proof responses earn mastery of that specific objective. Your saved checks and completion date remain available to review.\n\nBRING WHAT YOU ALREADY KNOW\nAn optional placement check samples each objective and suggests where to begin. It can open a later starting point; it never awards lesson mastery or claims to measure your overall ability.\n\nSEE YOUR PROGRESS\nResume unfinished learning from Home. Follow recommendations that explain why a course is suggested. Search course names, ideas and lesson text. Open your Knowledge Map to move from subjects to courses, units and objectives, with progress drawn from your saved work.\n\nMADE FOR YOUR MAC\n• 10 Foundation courses, 20 units and 40 objectives\n• 160 practice, proof and placement questions\n• Light, dark and system appearance, plus larger reading text\n• Keyboard shortcuts for search, settings and back navigation\n• Learning saved locally, with a recovery copy\n• Offline lessons and optional reference links that open in your browser\n• No account, advertising, subscription, analytics or AI service; an optional one-time purchase unlocks all courses\n\nThis edition offers courses across Money, Technology, Career, Life Skills and Humanities. Business, Communication, Science and Creative are clearly marked as planned subjects with no lessons yet.\n\nOld Dog provides focused introductions, not professional qualifications. Its short checks record the understanding tested in each objective, not broad practical expertise or lasting retention. Financial examples are fictional and simplified. Household topics teach safe observation and when to seek qualified help.\n\nOld Dog. New Tricks.", "languageCodesISO2A":["EN"], "fileSizeBytes":"1084901", "formattedPrice":"Free", "userRatingCountForCurrentVersion":0, "trackContentRating":"4+", "averageUserRatingForCurrentVersion":0, "bundleId":"com.koinophobia.olddog", "sellerName":"BLAKE JIHAD TAYLOR", "userRatingCount":0}, 
