"description":"Keep a record of what you are praying through, in your own words.\n\nPreaching to the Choir is a private prayer journal for writing, recording, and returning to prayers over time. Begin with a sentence or a spoken prayer. Come back later to read what you wrote or hear your own voice again.\n\nWRITE OR RECORD\nWrite a prayer or record it with the microphone. Optional on-device transcription is available for supported devices and languages. You can keep and listen to a recording without a transcript.\n\nRETURN TO YOUR RECORD\nBrowse your dated journal, search your words, and revisit earlier prayers. Add reflection notes as your understanding changes. Names, labels, and threads help you organize the record in a way that makes sense to you.\n\nKEEP A COPY\nExport prayers and recordings through the system share sheet. Full-record exports offer an optional passphrase. Recently Deleted lets you restore a deleted prayer for 30 days, and Settings includes an option to erase the app's local record.\n\nPRIVATE AND PERSONAL\nNo account is required. Prayer text and audio are stored locally, and the app does not collect analytics, show ads, or track you. An optional device-authentication lock helps protect access to your journal. This version does not offer iCloud sync; device backups and copies you choose to export follow your device and destination settings.\n\nOPTIONAL KEEPER\nKeeper adds Similar wording in search and a Year view for revisiting one calendar year of your record. Choose a monthly or annual subscription, or a one-time lifetime purchase. Family Sharing is supported. Prayer capture, reading, exact search, and export remain free. If a subscription ends, your record stays readable and Years opened as a member remain open.\n\nPrivacy policy: https://koinophobialabs.com/preaching-to-the-choir/privacy\nTerms of use: https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/", "languageCodesISO2A":["EN"], "fileSizeBytes":"11831296", "formattedPrice"